Regression bug (pre-existing, NOT introduced by NEARS-3527's fix):
CustomRoleController::edit() 500s instead of a graceful 404 when the
requested role id belongs to a DIFFERENT store than the logged-in vendor.

Repro: as vendor ts@ts.com (store_id=35), GET
/vendor-panel/custom-role/edit/1 where role id=1 belongs to store_id=19.

`EmployeeRole::where('store_id',Helpers::get_store_id())->where(['id'=>$id])
->first(['id','name','modules'])` correctly returns null (store scoping is
NOT broken — no cross-store data is exposed or mutated), but
vendor-views/custom-role/edit.blade.php then dereferences `$role['name']`
unconditionally, producing an unhandled null-array-offset ViewException.

Live backend log line (Admin/storage/logs/laravel.log, this worktree's own
QA-session server, PII-safe):

  [2026-09-13 04:59:47] production.ERROR: [FAIL] Trying to access array offset
  on null (View: /Users/Apple/Projects/nears-NEARS-3527-vendorapp-customrole-modules-whitelist/Admin/resources/views/vendor-views/custom-role/edit.blade.php)
  {"trace_id":"208ed614a6d55b271575cc8113a7a4c8",
   "correlation_id":"90a619a6-691e-4d16-87a2-28da611ec496",
   "type":"Illuminate\\View\\ViewException",
   "endpoint":"/vendor-panel/custom-role/edit/1"}

Scope note: the diff for this ticket touches ONLY store()'s and update()'s
inline validate() rules — edit()'s null-handling and the blade are byte-
identical before and after this fix. Confirmed as pre-existing, unrelated to
this ticket's own scope (which explicitly excludes "any other Vendor/
Store-Panel controller" changes). Filed as a regression_bug, non-blocking for
this ticket's PASS verdict.

Suggested fix (for whoever picks this up): guard edit() with
`abort_if(!$role, 404)` (or an equivalent `optional($role)`/`$role?->name`
null-safe access in the blade) before rendering — the SAME shape of fix as
would be needed for a well-behaved 404 anywhere else this
`where('store_id',...)->first()` pattern is used unguarded.
